WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.150
I'm in Crystal Palace Park, in south London,
and there are dinosaurs.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.400
Models of dinosaurs, anyway.
And inaccurate models at that:

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.019
but that's because they're
more than 150 years old.

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:15.749
These were the first ever lifesize models
of extinct creatures,

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:18.000
built for the gardens
of the enormous Crystal Palace

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.750
that used to stand
on top of that hill over there.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:24.460
They were made by the wonderfully-named
Benjamin Waterhouse Hawkins,

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:27.810
we now know that they are utterly wrong
in many significant ways,

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.850
but at the time they were a marvel:

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:31.580
look at what once walked the earth!

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:36.540
Now, in England, there's a list of buildings
that have special protection under the law.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:40.410
Buildings on that list are called...
Listed Buildings.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.120
Because they're on the list.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.280
Of buildings.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.760
And this country's full of them: Historic
England,

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:48.640
the not-quite-government organisation
that manages the list,

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.370
says there's about
half a million buildings on it.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:52.920
Most of those are only Grade 2 listed,

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.630
which means they've got to be
kept mostly intact,

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.640
and any changes need
a really good reason behind them,

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:01.390
but more than 10,000 places
are Grade 1 listed,

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:03.219
which means they must be preserved.

00:01:03.219 --> 00:01:07.499
Pretty much anything that was built more than 200 years ago and is still standing is on the list,

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.780
but there are some more modern things too...
including these dinosaurs.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:17.110
Yep. Grade 1 listed dinosaurs.
Can't be changed, moved, or demolished,

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.369
have to kept in good condition.

00:01:18.369 --> 00:01:23.780
And they can't be updated to reflect what
modern palaeontologists know,

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.360
because that would involve changing them,

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.600
and destroying not a dinosaur display --

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:32.170
but a display about what we
once thought dinosaurs looked like,

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:36.200
something that's notable not
because of what it represents in itself,

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.240
but because of the history in the sculptures.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:43.650
These dinosaurs must, by law,
remain inaccurate,

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.689
because the story they tell
isn't about prehistoric times...

00:01:46.689 --> 00:01:49.400
it's about science, just 150 years ago.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:53.290
I've done a video with Minute Earth about
Null Island,

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:55.040
the busiest place that doesn't exist.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.290
You can check go it out on their channel.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.300
